== H6
# H6: SITE = plan3/walk_sites.txt's 51 (= g2a m_hits_calls.tsv less scope.rs:35 :77
# :145) ; HIER / RTN / PROBE = the three the 51 lack (g3 REPORT K5 N1) ; INTERNAL =
# the walk's own body.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-3 (2026-11-24, the read side): held.rs clk_refused_at's `refused` closure compares at_text(&r.alias) (LEAVE L9, DK1-4b): its hit set names the call.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the walk moves into lexscope/walk.rs (MOVE 8, R-G15) — its 5 INTERNAL / PROBE rows re-homed, hand columns kept
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24): the walk hands its candidate as an AtKey (DELTA16 E1.3, E1.4) — the two closure pairs: edge_gate.rs binding_encloses' second walk probes through `other_kind_at` (the typed twin ; `other_kind` stays for the found text key), held.rs clk_refused_at through `refused_at` (at_same: the candidate against a refused alias ; `refused` / at_text stays for the found key) ; both pairs' candidate halves leave at DK2. walk_scopes' INTERNAL `table` row holds by PROBE_METHODS + `contains_at` (R-H8 (b)).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-2 (2026-11-24): FOUND rows (R-H8 (g), engine edit: `found_key_closure`) — a closure that reads a walk's found key (a DeclKey) is no walk hit, so no SITE row held its stores: the found-key copy of each E1.4 pair gets its own row (edge_gate.rs binding_encloses `other_kind()`, held.rs clk_refused_at `refused()` ; their candidate copies stay the SITE rows' `other_kind_at()` / `refused_at()`)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 (2026-11-25, DELTA17 F6 (3)): two found-key closures bound to ONE name in one fn (a shadowing `let`) FAIL the test (`H6 DUP FOUND`)
# in place of the silent collapse to one FOUND row ; on this tree there is none.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 round 2 (W/scopebind/dk1_6/r2/claims.tsv): a closure bound through `&`, a paren or a block's tail (`let c = { let p = ..;
# move |k: &DeclKey| .. };`) is a local / found-key closure ; an untyped closure whose parameter goes to found_text / key_same /
# gen_binding_encloses or a `_found` entry reads a FOUND key (FOUND_FNS / FOUND_METHODS ; every lexscope fn with a DeclKey parameter must be
# one: `H6 FOUND TAKER`) ; two local closures bound to ONE name in one fn while a probe calls `name()` FAIL (`H6 DUP LOCAL`) ; none on this tree.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26, form (c)): a site calls a NAMED ENTRY of lexscope/walk.rs, one per hit set (E-1c ; the entry column), its hit text the entry's arm (E-2c, table H6A) ; the 51 SITE rows' hit_set stands but held.rs clk_refused_at's (`at_same()` was the deleted local closure's free call ; a `hit_*` lane is read by its fields: clk_refused+symbols) ; site_texts 25 -> 23 (one text per entry), site_sets 20 ; walk_scopes deleted (its INTERNAL row gone) ; an entry's own walk call is its arm, H6A's row, not a SITE
