== H6A
# H6A (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2, form (c), E-2c ; DELTA19C J2 L1, q26): one row per NAMED ENTRY of lexscope/walk.rs (E-1c: a non-private fn
# of the file that is ONE call of one of the four generic walks with a closure literal last) — the entry ; kind = the walk it calls ;
# arm_text = probes_of(its closure) in source order ; order = the arm text with each `hit_*` lane replaced by its own fields in source
# order (the `||` order a site spelled before DK2) ; set = the store set ; sites = the H6 SITE calls of the entry. Rules in the h6 test:
# H6 ENTRY FORM (A1c with P71: every non-private fn of the file but is_gen_scope_segment), H6 ARM BLIND (A2, on the closure), H6 ENTRY
# UNUSED (A4), H6 HIT HOME (A6). Not seen (REVIEW-ONLY, scope_home.rs head ; NP19-4): a guard, a negation or a formed key inside an
# entry's closure (its SURF_BODY hash is the pin), `&&` for `||` or a negation inside a lane, a field probed twice in one lane.
# NOT-PROMISED (one shape a line ; measured by the negative controls of plan19/s8b M7 and §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2's M7, W/scopebind/dk2/m7/SUMMARY.txt):
#  NP19-1 two entry calls of one fn swapped (ident_route.rs bare_ident_route's walk_key_any_const_or_net :99 / walk_key_value :122, control swap_ir exchanges the two):
#         every table passes ; H6 counts each entry per fn and holds no order (behaviour pins only).
#  NP19-2 a guard or a helper added in a LANE's body (bound/read.rs, held.rs: outside the file set, no SURF_BODY hash): np2b `&& self.zz_guard()`,
#         np2c a nested fn negating at_same in hit_clk_refused, np2d `self.clk_refused.len() < 2 &&` pass every table ; np2a (the lane through a
#         private helper) moves H6 + H6A. The same three shapes inside an ENTRY's closure ARE seen: e2b H6 ARM BLIND + SURF BODY, e2c H6 + H6A +
#         SURF BODY, e2d H6 ARM BLIND + SURF BODY / OUT-C / OUT-F.
#  NP19-4 a guard, a negation or a formed key inside an entry's closure passes A1c / A2 ; SURF_BODY moves at least: g1 (`if name.starts_with('$')`)
#         HSEG + BODY + OUT-C, g2 (`!self.symbols.contains_at(k)`) BODY only, g3 (`&& !name.is_empty()`) BODY + OUT-C, g4 (`AtKey(name.to_string())`)
#         H6 + H6A + HKC + BODY.
