== HM
# HM: the mints of scope-qualified text, by (file, fn, mint kind, name) with a count — g3 mints.tsv's rule
# (census_g3.rs + link.py): `call` a call of a mint fn (MINT_CALLS), `fmt` / `fmt-tempname` a `format!` /
# `write!` glue literal holding `.` or `$` (a temp-name prefix or no scope marker = `fmt-tempname`), `join` a
# `.join(".")`, `push` a `push('.')` / `push('$')` or a `push_str` in display_of / walk_out_from / gen_rtn_key,
# `curp` a `<recv>.cur_prefix.clone()` ; `derived-fn` rows are HAND (G3's compile probe named them: a fn that
# returns text its body mints ; the test checks the fn exists). 375 by syntax (strings.rs:139's `matches!` guard
# among them, G3's M386) + 11 HAND = 386. TAG (hand, per mint, `a=n+b=m` when a row holds two): key, scope,
# segment (a `$…$` scope segment or a relative chain of them), display, spelling — g4 OWED-a's 20 glue rows,
# from_what "AST path segments" / "a deferred hier path" = spelling (DELTA6 DK1), the rest by reading T.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-2a: the 15 declaration-side `fq` calls of DELTA15 C1.3 (+ net_util.rs:656, N11-4) and frames_reserve.rs's two
# written-out forms are `self.lex.new_key(..)` (call fq 88 -> 73 by MINT_CALLS ; fmt: the two `{}.{}` key formats -> lexscope/key.rs
# new_key's one) ; MINT_CALLS does not list new_key: the mint lives inside lexscope (HX at DK1-6 reads the entry)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-2b: the 8 body-scope saved-key mints (generate.rs:167 :262 :699 :711 :736, net_util.rs:604, package.rs:530
# :549) are `self.lex.new_key(..)`: call fq 73 -> 65
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-2c: the 17 Bound mints (package.rs:779 :971 :1396 :1465 :1517 :1605, instance.rs:170 :718 :727 :764 :807,
# iface_inst.rs:152 :566, params.rs:1876 :1922 :1929 :2387) are `self.lex.new_key(..)`: call fq 65 -> 48 ; instance.rs's 4 left
# (:986 :1031 :1061 :1067) are read-side probes (DK1-3)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-3 (2026-11-24, the read side): the 48 read-side `fq` calls are `self.lex.at_cur(..)` (an AtKey, 38 reads + held.rs's alias + ports.rs's two glues) or
# `scope_out(self.lex.show_miss(..))` (7 message / IR-constant texts) and `fq` is deleted: call fq 48 -> 0 (MINT_CALLS keeps `fq`:
# a planted call is a NEW ROW) ; fmt: scope.rs fq's `{}.{}` -> lexscope/key.rs at_cur's (key) and show_miss's (display)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the walk moves into lexscope/walk.rs (MOVE 8, R-G15) — its 9 mint rows re-homed (TAG kept)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5a (2026-11-25): the five movers' 11 mint rows re-homed to lexscope/hier.rs (kind, count, TAG kept) ; key_in (key.rs) `<k>.<member>` NEW, key ; ports.rs elaborate_virtual_iface fmt 2 -> 1: the src glue is key_in's, the dst `format!("{vif}.{m}")` is handed to new_key (the 4th composite mint, DELTA17 F4: vif = the handle's declared name, m = a member name of the interface declaration) — totals unchanged
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b (2026-11-25): decl_keep_snapshot's `format!("{prefix}.")` (the package scope's text and its dot) is keys_under_cur's (lexscope/mod.rs ; TAG scope kept) — every mint of the snapshot is inside the module [DK1-6 (2026-11-25): ROUND 1's form, never built — the round-2 line below is the built state (newreads N9 (b))]
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b round 2 (2026-11-25, the cost trip on the package path): that `format!` is gone: the prefix test reads the current text and the byte after it (`k.starts_with(prefix)` and `as_bytes()[prefix.len()] == b'.'`), no `<prefix>.` text is formed ; its HM row `keys_under_cur fmt format 1` is gone
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26, form (c)): the 51 walk calls call their NAMED ENTRY (MINT_CALLS knows the 23 by E-1c ; TAG key as the walk rows) — 46 site rows re-keyed (the five two-walk fns split 2 -> 1+1), walk_scopes' `call walk_scopes_key` row gone, + 23 rows `lexscope/walk.rs <entry> call <its walk> 1 key`
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a (2026-11-26): bind_iface_port's two prefix formats move to lexscope/elab.rs alias_iface_port (TAG scope kept)
