# HSEG: the segment-text tests — a text method (SEG_METHODS) whose literal argument holds `.` `$` `[` or `::`,
# every `strip_prefix` (g4 OWED-d's domain), a `starts_with` / `strip_prefix` / `ends_with` / `strip_suffix`
# with a non-literal argument (`<…>` = its reduced form), and every call of is_gen_scope_segment ; by (file, fn,
# method, argument) with a count. The plan's 22 + 6 + 3 lines and G4's 28 sites were predictions ; this is
# the number (W15). TAG (hand): scope (a scope path's text), key, spelling (a source / compiler name, a
# literal), display ; UNIT (hand, the unit that takes the test): walk (the walk family's text, DK1 / DK2), LS2
# (scope_chain_abs, LS2-d), LS4 (a named text entry), DK1 (a mint body), DK3, DK4, RS1, `-` (not a scope test) ; since LS3b-1 /
# LS4 also the unit that DELETES a test already inside lexscope: B3k (kind / parent tests), B3a (a key cut to its scope).
# DK1-0 (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY, DELTA14 D1, R-F3, premise10 J7 / N10-7): scope_chain_abs LS2 -> B3k ; gen_binding_encloses DK3 -> B3a ;
# names_with_pkg_var_aliases, decl_keep_snapshot DK3 -> DK1 (DK1-5b moved names_with_pkg_var_aliases in ; decl_keep_snapshot stayed
# in decl_scope.rs and asks the module one scope question, keys_under_cur, R-J1) ; disp.rs cur_context, display_of DK4 -> B3k ;
# enter_frame_scope_root, stmt_loc_instance DK4 -> `-` (they drop the `%m` absolute marker: no scope kind or parent read).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the walk moves into lexscope/walk.rs (MOVE 8, R-G15) — its 7 segment tests re-homed (TAG scope, UNIT walk kept)
