== H5
# H5: the name-typed fields — census_fields.rs's rule: the structs reached from Elaborator and ConstFrame
# through field types (aliases expanded), each field whose type names String / str / Symbol / Ident ; 215 =
# g1 fields.tsv row for row, type text equal. CLASS / CODE (hand) = g1's (BINDING V R T S ; NOT D CTX I INPUT
# COPY DEF G CHK X). STORE (hand) = what the field holds as key or value: KEYED-PLAN26 / -JUDGE5 / -OTHER
# (g3 fields_keyed.tsv's in_list ; ClkRefused.alias = JUDGE5's clk_refused), ROUTINE (G4 OWED-r's 14, a
# first pass), SCOPE (cur_prefix, LS3's 6 Elaborator fields, G4 OWED-b's 16 record fields), DISPLAY
# (frame_func_names G4 g4-5, expr_scopes, stmt_scopes, the 3 display-chain fields), OUTPUT (ProcIdent.scope),
# KEY (CovgInstMeta.inst, a covergroup declaration key), `-` (holds no minted key or scope text).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-1: the 32 String-keyed KEYED fields are `Keyed<V>` / `KeyedSet` (window w9, lexscope/key.rs) — their rows
# keep CLASS / CODE / STORE, the type column is the window's (H5 reads WINDOW_TYPES as name-typed) ; KEYED-W9 = the two
# window types' own inner map / set, which hold every binding of those 32 stores (CODE V for the holder ; the field rows keep theirs).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-2a: NewKey's own field (lexscope/key.rs) is a declaration key's text (KEY ; CODE I, pattern_targets' row's) ;
# pattern_targets' value holds a NewKey (lib.rs:336), so its row left (a retype to a key type) — KEYED-OTHER 6 -> 5, KEY 1 -> 2.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-2b: gen_genvars' element (lib.rs:1129) and lexscope's gen_text genvar key (mod.rs:82) are NewKeys (a retype
# to a key type: both rows left — KEYED-OTHER 5 -> 4, SCOPE 5 -> 4) ; rtn_decl_genvars keeps its ROUTINE key (RS1), its value's
# element is a NewKey (R-G3: the type column moved, the row stays).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-3 (2026-11-24, the read side): AtKey's own field (lexscope/key.rs) is a read key's text (KEY ; CODE I, NewKey's) ; ClkRefused.alias holds an AtKey
# (held.rs:356, its one producer, was an `fq` read key: N11-3), so its row left (a retype to a key type) — KEYED-JUDGE5 5 -> 4, KEY 2 -> 3.
struct	file	field	type	CLASS	CODE	STORE
