# HOUT: where display / child-prefix text goes (LS1 part 4 ; DELTA9 J4 + DELTA10 L5) — by (file, fn, what,
# arg, sink) with a count: every call of display_prefix / display_of / scope_chain_abs / frame_path /
# frame_path_of / cur_context / child_prefix / enter_frame_scope_root (arg = the arguments' tokens) ; the
# `ProcIdent {` / `InstanceInfo {` / `CovgInstMeta {` literals (arg = the scope field's initializer) ; the
# saves of the three display fields (`mem::take` / `mem::replace` of `&mut <recv>.F`, `<recv>.F.replace(..)`,
# and `via f(..)`: a call of a fn whose save is its return, enter_frame_scope_root) and their restores
# (`<recv>.F = <a local a save bound>`) ; push_func's `m_path` argument (`local <- its let initializer`) ; the
# `reported` set's `let` and parameters (`BTreeSet<(u32, u32, String)>`). SINK = the first consumer above
# the value (`&`, `( )`, `?`, a cast, Some / Ok / Err / Box::new and .clone / .to_string / .to_owned / .into /
# .unwrap_or_default see through): LOCAL:<name>#<the identifier's tokens in the fn>, FIELD:<Struct.field>,
# ARG:<callee> (a method's receiver tokens + name), RECV:.<method>, ASSIGN:<lhs>, RET, MAC:<macro>><outer>,
# CLOSURE><outer>, BIN / COND / STMT / OTHER. Equal on T to copies.tsv's H01-H13, H28, H30 destinations, the
# 9 saves and 9 restores of DELTA10 L2, push_func's 3 producers, the set's 3 lines (LS1 part 4 REPORT).
# LS2-d: the callees add the typed shims, LEAVE L4 display_of_key_text (L4 closed at §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a: private, its one
# call inside lexscope/disp.rs net_name_table), stmt_loc_instance, shown_from_spelling,
# scope_out (a call, or `scope_out` handed on as a value: arg `fn-value`) and `.plain()` ; a SAVE is also a call of
# a Saved* entry (disp_chain_take / disp_chain_swap_single / disp_root_swap_empty / disp_enter_frame_root /
# disp_root_swap_decl_inst / disp_class_method_swap) and a RESTORE a disp_*_restore(<local>) ; the display fields
# are read as `<recv>.lex.F` too (disp_chain / disp_root / disp_method).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a (2026-11-26): net_name_table's display_of_key_text row re-homed (lexscope/disp.rs) ; + 4 `scope_out` fn-value rows: its Vec<Shown> leaves through api.rs, and the three by-id diagnostics (cont_var.rs, lvalue.rs, netdecl.rs) print net_key_shown's Shown
