== HC_CARRY_LOCAL
# HC CARRY LOCAL (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-0 ; DELTA14 D8 q2, R-F2, R-F10, premise10 J4 / N10-3): the carries bound by `let` (SINK
# LOCAL:<name>#<uses>) the HC_CARRY test admits, by (file, fn, entry, SINK) with a count. Each is the PARENT scope taken before the
# child instance is entered (scope_swap to the child), handed to wire_ports and re-entered there by `scope_swap` only (P34: never
# asked a question, never turned to text) ; until DK1-0 the same value was the bridge's text (HBR rows LOCAL:parent#2 /
# LOCAL:parent_prefix#2). A LOCAL carry off this list fails, a listed row with no carry fails (STALE), and HC_CARRY_COUNTS'
# `local` must equal the listed count. W12: this list may only fall.
file	fn	entry	sink	count
