== HKI
# HKI (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 (2026-11-25), DELTA18 R-J9 NOTE-2 ; engine test hki_the_key_in_callers_are_pinned): every call of lexscope's
# `key_in(k, member)` outside lexscope, by (file, fn, entry) with a count — key_in forms the member key `<k>.<member>` with no empty-key
# guard (its doc), so a second caller is a new row whose key must be read. §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 round 2 (W/scopebind/dk1_6/r2/claims.tsv):
# key_in named as a value (`let mk = key_in;`, `.map(lexscope::key_in)`) is a caller too (args `fn-value`) ; a closure's body, a `matches!`
# guard's scrutinee and `vec![e; n]`'s element are read (mac_exprs: a comma list, else the first expression).
# NOT-PROMISED (one shape a line):
#  K1 `use crate::lexscope::key_in as member_key; member_key(&k, m)`: a `use .. as` rename is no watched name.
#  K2 a `#[cfg(test)]` fn's call outside lexscope: test code is no caller of the program (watched_calls reads no cfg(test) fn).
#  K3 `zz! { .. key_in(&k, m) .. }`: a macro's tokens after its first expression, or tokens that begin with no expression (a macro body).
#  K4 a call inside lexscope: not this table's (the module's own calls are its fns' bodies, SURF BODY-ALL).
file	fn	entry	count
ports.rs	elaborate_virtual_iface	key_in	1
