== HKC
# HKC (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24), DELTA16 R-H8 (d)): how many times each lexscope file names a key type's constructor (a call, a struct literal,
# a pattern, a macro argument) — AtKey's field is `pub(super)` since DK1-4b-1 (the walk forms its candidates: walk.rs), so its
# constructor door is the whole module ; NewKey's stays private to key.rs. A new row or a moved count is a key formed in a new
# place: P23 reads where its text comes from.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-2 (2026-11-24) (engine edit (b), R-H9 note 1): four columns — a form per row: `ctor` the constructor named (as before), `value` the type's path
# used as a value (`.map(AtKey)`, `let mk = AtKey`), `alias` a `type` alias or a `use .. as` rename, `write` the key's field `.0` written
# through a binding the fn types as the key ; the walk's scratch writes are pinned (walk.rs AtKey write 5: `key.0.clear()` x2,
# `push_str` x1, `write!(key.0, ..)` x2) ; DeclKey's constructions: walk.rs 3 (the three returns), tests.rs 1 (the cfg(test) helper).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5a (2026-11-25): key_in forms `<k>.<member>` from a read key (key.rs AtKey ctor 2 -> 3) ; Scopes::key_under returns an AtKey (mod.rs AtKey ctor 2: its two returns, the text the carried scope's interner holds + the name)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 (2026-11-25, DELTA17 F6 (3)): `Self` inside a key type's own impl, inherent or trait, counts as that type (`Self(s)` ctor,
# `Self { .. }` ctor, `let Self(t)` ctor, `.map(Self)` value ; `Self::new()` not) — on this tree it adds 0 (no key impl in lexscope names `Self` so).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 round 2 (W/scopebind/dk1_6/r2/claims.tsv): a `.0` write through a `Self`-typed binding of a key type's impl (`let mut k =
# Self(..)`, `k: &mut Self`), through `&mut self` of a key type's TRAIT impl, and `Self(..)` as `matches!`'s pattern are counted ; 0 on this tree.
# NOT-PROMISED (one shape a line):
#  C1 `type Me = Self; Me(s)` / `use super::AtKey as Hk` inside a fn body naming `Self`: an alias of `Self` (a module-level `type`/`use .. as` of
#     a key type IS the alias row).  (Any new or edited lexscope fn is still a new SURF BODY row: r2/neg M_HKC_ALIAS_SELF failed
#     ht_surf_the_lexscope_surface_is_pinned only.)
#  C2 a `.0` write through a binding whose type is not spelled where HKC reads it: an untyped `let` of a returned key, a struct field holding a
#     key, a `&mut String` taken by a method HKC_MUT does not list.
#  C3 a key formed in a macro body or a `macro_rules!` definition (tokens no expression list nor `matches!` form).
#  C4 a whole-key move (`mem::swap` of two keys moves a key, not its text).
file	type	form	count
lexscope/key.rs	AtKey	ctor	3
lexscope/key.rs	NewKey	ctor	2
lexscope/mod.rs	AtKey	ctor	2
lexscope/tests.rs	DeclKey	ctor	1
lexscope/walk.rs	AtKey	ctor	3
lexscope/walk.rs	AtKey	write	5
lexscope/walk.rs	DeclKey	ctor	3
== HKC_COUNTS
ctor[AtKey=8 DeclKey=4 NewKey=2] value[AtKey=0 DeclKey=0 NewKey=0] alias[AtKey=0 DeclKey=0 NewKey=0] write[AtKey=5 DeclKey=0 NewKey=0]
